==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gmh|de}} {{term|schicken||to outfit oneself, fit in, arrange appropriately|lang=gmh}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{m|gem-pro|*skikkijaną||to order, send}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|de}} {{m|ine-pro|*skeg-||to jump, spring}}; representing the causative of {{etyl|gmh|de}} {{term|geschehen|geschehen, geschēn|to happen, rush|lang=gmh}} from {{etyl|goh|de}} {{term|giskehan||to happen|lang=goh}} from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{m|gem-pro|*skehaną||to run, move quickly}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|de}} {{m|ine-pro|*skek-||to run, jump, spring}}. Akin to {{etyl|ang|-}} {{m|ang|scēon||to happen}}, ''schie-'' in {{etyl|nl|-}} {{term|schielijk||hasty|lang=nl}}. More at {{term|chic|lang=en}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈʃɪkŋ̩/|/ˈʃɪkən/|lang=de}}
* {{audio|De-schicken.ogg|audio (Germany)|lang=de}}
* {{audio|De-at-schicken.ogg|audio (Austria)|lang=de}}
* {{rhymes|ɪkŋ̩|lang=de}}

